 "findings":[
  {"heading":"Modify theme / Modificar el tema","segment_index":"S28.P2","kind":"untrue","en_span":"chapters/ggplot_basics.qmd:699-699","tr_span":"chapters/ggplot_basics.es.qmd:705-705","proposition":"The theme() reference table says plot.caption = element_text() adjusts the legend (\"La leyenda\"), whereas the English says it adjusts the caption.","reader_consequence":"A Spanish reader looking for the argument that styles the plot legend picks plot.caption and changes the caption text instead; the same reader also loses the table's only pointer to the caption argument, because everywhere else in this chapter 'leyenda' denotes the ggplot legend and 'pie del gráfico' denotes the caption.","confidence":"medium"},
  {"heading":"Free or fixed axes / Ejes libres o fijos","segment_index":"S19.P1","kind":"code_mismatch","en_span":"chapters/ggplot_basics.qmd:489-489","tr_span":"chapters/ggplot_basics.es.qmd:494-494","proposition":"The translation names the argument as `scale = \"free\"`, while the English names `scales = \"free\"` and the code chunk beside it uses `facet_wrap(~District, scales = \"free\")`.","reader_consequence":"A reader who copies `scale = \"free\"` into facet_grid() gets an ignored/unknown argument, the axes stay fixed, and `space = \"free_y\"` silently has no effect.","confidence":"high"},
  {"heading":"Scaled to column values / Escalado a los valores de la columna","segment_index":"S13.P1","kind":"untrue","en_span":"chapters/ggplot_basics.qmd:266-266","tr_span":"chapters/ggplot_basics.es.qmd:268-268","proposition":"The translation says the alternative is to plot objects with sizes proportional to their column values, restricting the mechanism to the size aesthetic; the English says any plot aesthetic can be scaled by the values in a column.","reader_consequence":"A reader concludes that only size can be driven by a column, which contradicts the section's own first example (color mapped to age) and discourages mapping color, shape or alpha to data.","confidence":"medium"},
  {"heading":"Plot aesthetics / Estética del gráfico","segment_index":"S11.P1","kind":"untrue","en_span":"chapters/ggplot_basics.qmd:228-228","tr_span":"chapters/ggplot_basics.es.qmd:228-228","proposition":"The translation says `color =` sets the colour of the point's perimeter (\"el color del perimetro del punto\") when using geom_point(); the English says it sets the point colour.","reader_consequence":"A reader expects color= to draw only an outline on points and reaches for fill= to colour the dot, which does nothing for the default point shape, so the points come out unchanged.","confidence":"medium"},
  {"heading":"Import data / Importar datos","segment_index":"S4.P2","kind":"added","en_span":"chapters/ggplot_basics.qmd:55-55","tr_span":"chapters/ggplot_basics.es.qmd:55-55","proposition":"The translation states that ct_blood holds the cycle-threshold value of the PCR test (\"cycle threshold, umbral de ciclo del test de PCR\"); the English says only \"CT values\".","reader_consequence":"The Spanish reader is given an interpretation of the variable that the English text never asserts, so the two editions disagree on what ct_blood measures and the claim is not verifiable from the handbook itself.","confidence":"medium"},
  {"heading":"Resources / Recursos","segment_index":"S44.P1","kind":"added","en_span":"chapters/ggplot_basics.qmd:1167-1167","tr_span":"chapters/ggplot_basics.es.qmd:1170-1170","proposition":"The translation adds that the listed pages carry material in English (\"Consulta las siguietnes páginas con maerial en inglés\"); the English text makes no claim about the language of the resources.","reader_consequence":"A Spanish reader who avoids English-language material skips the whole list, even though two of the listed links point to the Spanish edition of R for Data Science (es.r4ds.hadley.nz), so the added claim is contradicted by the list beneath it.","confidence":"medium"}
 ]}
